Done. #817 is closed.

What was wrong: auto_context_for_prompt scored repo files, read them with a bare std::fs::read_to_string, and repl.rs prepended the content to the prompt — i.e. straight into the API request. grep -n 'dir_restrictions\|check_path' src/commands_project.rs returned zero matches, while `src/tools.rs:1069/1208 wrap every model-facing read tool in maybe_guard`. So the same file was **refused when the model asked for it** and **silently attached to the same request** when auto-context picked it, under a green 📎 Auto-attached: note.

What I changed:
• auto_context_for_prompt(prompt, recent_context, restrictions: &DirectoryRestrictions) — filter through restrictions.check_path before the read loop, beside the existing binary-extension skip. A denied file is never opened, never consumes one of the three AUTO_CONTEXT_MAX_FILES slots, and never reaches the signature block (which is built from matched_paths, already filtered).
• src/repl.rs passes `&agent_config.dir_restrictions at the one non-test call site. No process-global; commands.rs` is a name re-export and needed no edit.
• check_path short-circuits to Ok when restrictions are empty, so the common product path is byte-identical.
• No refusal block printed — auto-context is a silent convenience the user did not ask for, unlike #748/#761 where the user asked for the refused thing.

Test: `test_auto_context_respects_directory_restrictions`, at the emission point (the vec a caller receives), in both directions in one test — denied path absent when denied, present with empty restrictions. I verified the near-miss branch actually executes rather than hitting the early return, by temporarily turning that return into a panic! and confirming it didn't fire.

Register: the diff pushed commands_project.rs 102 lines past its recorded entry (fatal, over the 100-line drift band), so GRANDFATHERED_OVERSIZED_MODULES was updated to 3298, and repl.rs's warning to 3357 — paid off in the task that caused it.

cargo fmt --check, clippy --all-targets -D warnings, build, test (5064 passed) all green. CLAUDE.md's commands_project.rs bullet updated, including the plain statement that permissions.deny (bash patterns) is a different mechanism and untouched.
